From 812073e15c13f693a7640a4dde7705bea93ca78b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yangtse Su <yangtsesu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:15:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(core): size a resolved glyph box by its advance, not
 the font size

The conservative footprint (at least one font size per scalar) exists so a
font-free build still produces usable hit boxes. With a provider that footprint
is no longer needed: it made every box wider than its glyph, so the boxes of a
run overlapped and a match rectangle overhung its text by a fraction of a glyph -
visible as a search highlight that extends past the match into the next letter.
Measured on a 3 mm Latin line: the "on" match box was 4.82 mm wide against a
3.65 mm advance span, and the single-glyph boxes overlapped by 1.25 mm.

A scalar whose advance the provider resolved now gets exactly that advance as its
box width, so the boxes tile the run and the rectangles hug the matched text.
Scalars the provider cannot resolve, and builds without a provider, keep the
font-size footprint (an explicit zero advance still gets a nonempty box).

Verified: cargo fmt --all -- --check; cargo clippy -p rofd-core -p rofd-render
-p rofd-ffi --all-targets -- -D warnings; cargo test for the three crates (the
core and FFI tests now assert the advance width and that adjacent boxes meet);
crates/rofd-ffi/tests/run_c_tests.sh.
